<section xml:id="review">
      <title>Review</title>

      <p>
        Let <m>W \subseteq \mathbb{R}^{n}</m> be a linear subspace, and consider
        <m>W_{\geq 0} = W \cap \mathbb{R}^{n}_{\geq 0}</m>. An <term>elementary vector</term>
        <m>\vec{w} \in W</m> is a nonzero vector that is support minimal in the sense that there does not
        exist another nonzero vector <m>\vec{u} \in W_{\geq 0}</m> such that
        <m>\text{supp}(\vec{u}) \subsetneq \text{supp}(\vec{w})</m>.
      </p>

      <exercise>
        <introduction>
          <p>
            Let <m>W \subseteq \mathbb{R}^{n}</m> be a linear subspace and
            <m>W_{\geq 0} = W \cap \mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}^{n}</m>.
          </p>
        </introduction>
        <task>
          <statement>
            <p>
              Show that the support of any nonzero vector in <m>W_{\geq 0}</m> contains the support of some elementary vector.
            </p>
          </statement>
        </task>
        <task>
          <statement>
            <p>
              Show that, for any nonzero vector <m>\vec{v} \in W_{\geq 0}</m>, there exists an elementary vector
              <m>\vec{u} \in W_{\geq 0}</m> such that <m>\vec{v} - \vec{u} \in W_{\geq 0}</m> and
              <m>\text{supp}(\vec{v} - \vec{u}) \subsetneq \text{supp}(\vec{v})</m>.
            </p>
          </statement>
        </task>
        <task>
          <statement>
            <p>
              Show that <m>W_{\geq 0}</m> is the set of non-negative linear combinations of its elementary vectors.
            </p>
          </statement>
        </task>
      </exercise>
    </section>